  "kp112-img-01.jpg":
    "Infographic: what science delivered. Why industrial production agriculture fails farmers, fails nature and fails the future, and how PQNK brings agriculture back to life. The reality industrial science created: soil degradation and hardpan, loss of organic matter, an imbalanced water cycle, a degraded climate, rising input dependency and production cost, stagnating yields, declining food quality, and farming that is not viable for smallholders. The problem was never the farmer; it was the model. The wrong question was how to get more from inputs; the right question is how nature produces abundantly without destroying the soil. The solution PQNK offers: no tillage, permanent living cover, no synthetic chemicals, a balanced ecological system, a restored water cycle, lower input and cost, higher and stable yields, better food quality, and farming that is viable for all. Nature is the original high-performance model. PQNK in action: orchards convert quickly with the hardpan broken, furrows outside the canopy, irrigation only when the trees show need, and permanent mulch; seasonal crops are planted without tillage with new no-till planters such as SIPP and VIPP; and hundreds of PQNK farmers now share their knowledge from field to field. The future of agriculture is working with nature's algorithms.",
